  "notes": "USAGE:\n- {差配|さはい}する (to manage, to supervise)\n- {差配|さはい}を{任|まか}される (to be entrusted with management)\n- {差配|さはい}{人|にん} (manager, agent)\n\nSENSE 2 (Historical):\nIn the Edo period and early modern Japan, {差配|さはい} or {差配人|さはいにん} referred to property managers who acted on behalf of landlords. This usage appears in historical fiction and period dramas.\n\nMODERN EQUIVALENTS:\n- {管理人|かんりにん} (building manager)\n- {不動産管理|ふどうさんかんり}{会社|かいしゃ} (property management company)\n\nRELATED:\n- {管理|かんり} (management)\n- {監督|かんとく} (supervision)\n- {取|と}り{仕切|しき}る (to manage, to direct)",
